# The ship comes alive (#249): the lantern lights the galley stove with a
# little of his own flame. Played by the ShipAwakening node in
# scenes/prototype/sea.tscn when you ask him at the stove. Placeholder
# writing: rewrite freely. His murmurs while you look for the stove, and the
# captain's few words, are in scripts/story/ship_awakening.gd and heron.dlg.
#
# The flag stove_lit is what lights it: setting it makes the flame pass, the
# lights come up from the galley outwards, and him go dimmer.

~ start
-> stove

~ stove
@go lantern stove_flame
@look lantern determined
lantern: ...Stove. Of course.
@wait 0.6
lantern: Just a little. It doesn't hurt.
@look lantern effort
@wait 0.8
set stove_lit
@wait 1.6
@look lantern tired
lantern: ...There.
lantern: ...Oh. That's... a bit dimmer than I'd planned.
@wait 0.6
lantern: Don't let it go out.
@home lantern
